# .mergeproofignore
#
# Paths listed here are excluded from merge-proof analysis: they are not
# counted as base-drift overlap and do not trigger protected-boundary
# findings.
#
# Syntax is gitignore-style: `#` comments, `*`, `**`, `?`, a leading `/` to
# anchor at the repository root, a trailing `/` for directories, and `!` to
# re-include a path a previous line excluded. Later lines win.
#
# merge-proof already excludes common generated and vendored output by
# default (lockfiles, dist/, build/, vendor/, node_modules/, *.min.js,
# *.generated.*, protobuf output). You do not need to list those.
#
# Use this file when a path is noisy in YOUR repository specifically.
# Excluding a path means giving up evidence about it, so prefer to keep the
# list short and to explain each entry.

# Docs churn constantly and rarely interacts with code changes.
# docs/**

# Generated API reference, rebuilt on every release.
# api-reference/**

# This repository IS CI tooling, so workflow files are the product and are
# reviewed as code rather than treated as a protected boundary.
# .github/workflows/**

# Fixture data that is rewritten wholesale by a generator.
# test/fixtures/**
# !test/fixtures/handwritten/**
